.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt MOUNT 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount ,
.Nm mount_nullfs
.Nd mount file systems
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl a
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl t Ar type Ns Op , Ns Ar type ...
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl t Ar type
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar special node
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Ar special | node
.Nm
.Fl -bind
.Ar directory node
.Nm mount_nullfs
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar target node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
attaches a file system to the directory
.Ar node ,
which then shows the file system's contents instead of its own, with
.Xr nmount 2 .
With no arguments it lists what is mounted.
.Pp
The file system types are:
.Bl -tag -width nullfs
.It Cm tmpfs
A new, empty file system in memory; its
.Ar special
is conventionally
.Dq tmpfs .
.It Cm nullfs
The directory
.Ar special
(the
.Ar target ) ,
seen again at
.Ar node ;
what is created or removed in one is in the other.
Linux calls this a bind mount, hence
.Fl -bind .
.El
.Pp
With a single
.Ar special
or
.Ar node ,
the rest is taken from its line in
.Xr fstab 5 .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Mount every file system in
.Xr fstab 5
that isn't mounted, isn't marked
.Cm noauto ,
and isn't the root, in the order listed.
.It Fl o Ar options
Comma-separated mount options.
.Cm rw
is the only one accepted for now; the kernel refuses others.
.It Fl t Ar type
The type to mount; with
.Fl a ,
the types to mount, or with a leading
.Dq no ,
the types not to.
.It Fl v
Name each file system mounted.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /proc/mounts -compact
.It Pa /etc/fstab
the file systems to mount
.It Pa /proc/mounts
what is mounted
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /mnt/scratch
mount -t nullfs /usr/src /mnt/src
mount_nullfs /usr/src /mnt/src
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nmount 2 ,
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr umount 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
command appeared in
.At v1 .
